{title: 596 - Look for the Waymarks}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #596 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 596}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Look for the way-marks as you journey on,
[Em]Look for the way-marks [D]passing one by one;
[G]Down through the ages, [C]past the kingdoms [Am]four—
[G]Where are we [C]stand[Am]ing? [D7]Look the way-marks [G]o’er.
[G]Look for the way-marks, the [Em]great prophetic [B]way-marks,
[C]Down through the ages, [D]past the kingdoms four.
[G]Look for the waymarks, the [Em]great prophetic [Am]way-marks;
The [G]journey’s al[D7]most [G]o’er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Look for the way-marks, the great prophetic way-marks,
[Em]Down through the ages, [D]past the kingdoms four.
[G]Look for [C]the waymarks, the [Am]great prophetic way-marks;
[G][C]The [Am]journey's [D7]almost [G]o'er.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]First, the Assyrian kingdom ruled the world,
[Em]Then Medo-Persia's [D]banners were unfurled;
[G]And after [C]Greece held [Am]universal sway,
[G]Rome [C]seized [Am]the scepter'where [D7]are [G]we today?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Down in the feet of iron and of clay,
[Em]Weak and divided, [D]soon to pass away;
[G]What will [C]the next great, [Am]glorious drama be?
[G]Christ [C]and [Am]His [D7]coming, [G]and eternity.
{end_of_verse}
